<td id="S5.T3.5.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T3.5.5.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">3,120</span></td>
<td id="S5.T3.5.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T3.5.5.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">1,657</span></td>
<td id="S5.T3.5.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T3.5.5.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">53.1%</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="S5.T3.6" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><span id="S5.T3.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;">Note: Possible erasures = instances <math id="S5.T3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> 5 models. Erasure rate = erased / possible.<span id="S5.T3.6.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 5.2. Differential Marker Vulnerability ‣ 5. Results ‣ When AI Writes, Whose Voice Remains? Quantifying Cultural Marker Erasure Across World English Varieties in Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> reveals pragmatic markers were erased at <span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">71.5%</span>, nearly double the lexical rate (37.1%), indicating implicit features are most vulnerable to alignment-driven standardization.</p>
</div>
